{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The safepoint fix checks out, including nested exit marks and explicit `:unmapped` refusal. The admission fix still has a blocker: it equates an index transaction number with an expander batch number and ignores the source medium and member index. Those counters can diverge, then accidentally match an older admission of identical content. I’m also checking whether the new publication fallback can mistake a missing user-call row for a synthesized wrapper."}}
